# REQUIRES: python-api, torch
# Forward-mode AD through mdir.torch is refused (D[torch-forward-refusal],
# #777), on the CPU, in double and mixed
# precision, Inputs/python_frames_torch_forward.py: torch.func.jvp,
# jacfwd, and torch.autograd.forward_ad, with the tangent on theta, the
# positions, the cells, and the tilts, of the energy and of
# gradients["positions"]; vmap of jvp; forward over reverse; under
# torch.compile. Each raises UnsupportedError naming forward mode and the
# tensor of the tangent, never a zero; torch.func.hessian stops in PyTorch's
# RuntimeError at its reverse level; a jvp whose tangent does not reach the
# operations is given; and the evaluator then gives the same gradients of
# reverse mode, to the bit.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %torch_python %S/Inputs/python_frames_torch_forward.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide CPU Double %t/double | FileCheck %s -DMODE="CPU Double"
# RUN: %torch_python %S/Inputs/python_frames_torch_forward.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide CPU Mixed %t/mixed | FileCheck %s -DMODE="CPU Mixed"
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: refused, UnsupportedError naming forward mode and the tensor of the tangent, never a zero: 19 forms
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: torch.func.hessian in theta and in the positions: RuntimeError of PyTorch at its reverse level, never a zero
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: a jvp whose tangent does not reach the operations gives the energy, to the bit
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: after the refusals, the gradients of reverse mode in theta, the positions, the cell, and of a loss on the forces in theta, to the bit: True
# CHECK: forward refusal passed
